    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Standardization and Decomposition: An Introduction for Social Scientists\"\nsubtitle: \"Workshop 15 July 2026\"\nauthor: \"Ben Matthews & Josiah King\"\n---\n\n\n\n\n\n\n# Overview\n\n#### When\n\nWednesday 15th July 2026  \n\n#### Where\n\n- In-person: University of Stirling, Cottrell Building, 2Y5. [Click here for the map!](https://link.mazemap.com/ioL7EsvH){target=\"_blank\"}  \n- Online: The session will be recorded and transcribed via Teams. If you are joining online please use the [link here](https://teams.microsoft.com/meet/330901632633208?p=fPyl1PD2AstUWviDs9){target=\"_blank\"}\n\n#### What to prepare?  \n\nPlease bring your own laptop with either R or Stata installed. If you cannot install either R or Stata on your own machine you will be able to complete practical exercises in R via a web browser, but for this you will need a free account with [posit.cloud](https://posit.cloud/){target=\"_blank\"}.  If you would like to use this \noption please sign up for an account at posit.cloud before the session.  \n\n\n# Schedule\n\n::::{.columns}\n:::{.column width=\"65%\"}\n__Sessions__  \n\n- [Welcome/Intro](lecture00.html)  \n- [Introduction to Standardisation and Decomposition](lecture-conceptual.html)  \n- [The whole game](lecture-whole-game.html)  \n- [Standardisation & Decomposition of Rates as Products](lecture-stddecompbasics.html)  \n- [Practical 1](workshop01.html)  \n- [Cross-classified Data & Multiple Populations](lecture-crossclass.html)  \n- [Practical 2](workshop02.html)  \n- [Uncertainty](lecture-uncertainty.html)  \n- [Practical 3](workshop03.html)\n\n<!-- [Other Methods of Decomposition](lecture-othermethods.html) -->\n\n:::\n:::{.column width=\"5%\"}\n:::\n:::{.column width=\"30%\"}\n__Breaks__  \n\n<br><br>\n11:00-11:15: Coffee  \n<br><br>\n12:15-13:15: Lunch  \n<br><br>\n14:15-14:30: Coffee\n\n:::\n::::\n\n",
